=== RATIFIED BASIS ===
N-9 "What It Binds": "T01.2.4 partial retraction: an object retaining at least
one valid upstream reference is re-versioned, not invalidated."
N-9 "Consequences Accepted": "A dependent supported by ten Facts, one of which
is invalidated, is handled by the partial-retraction rule rather than by
cascade -- the boundary between the two must be maintained carefully."
IOM 3.2: ACTIVE -> INVALIDATED on "All attesting Evidence retracted"; partial
retraction "produces a new version with reduced support, not invalidation.
The Fact remains attested."

Nothing beyond these was implemented. No threshold, vocabulary or behaviour
was invented.

=== SCOPE BOUNDARY OBSERVED ===
N-9 also states cascade performs NO interpretation and alters "status only,
never content". Cascade therefore does NOT create the reduced-support version:
producing a new version is the owning engine's act. Cascade applies the
boundary structurally -- it spares the object and REPORTS it via
CascadeResult.partially_retracted -- which is precisely "handled by the
partial-retraction rule rather than by cascade".

